WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:11.900
4. Who stole my money? I remember when a can of coke was 25 cents.

2
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:19.100
My parents could buy candy for a penny. Today, you might pay a dollar for a soda, and nothing

3
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:27.020
costs a penny. So, what happened? Inflation, that's what. Inflation is often called too

4
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:33.500
many dollars chasing too few goods. It's when prices in a country rise across the board.

5
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.540
If your favorite snack gets a bit more expensive, that's not inflation. But when the price of your

6
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:49.260
snack, bread, sugar, gasoline, and many other things all rise at the same time, that's inflation.

7
00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:53.500
Inflation means your money buys less than it used to.

8
00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:01.660
Experts have different views on why and how inflation happens. One reason for inflation

9
00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:08.380
is an increase in the supply of money. Generally, when the supply of something goes up, the demand

10
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:16.300
for it goes down. In other words, its value goes down. So, when there is a lot of money circulating,

11
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:23.020
each piece of money becomes less valuable. Another cause of inflation is a rise in production

12
00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:30.140
costs. This means it costs more money to make a particular product. The price of a candy bar

13
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:36.620
may go up if the nuts in it are suddenly more expensive, or if the workers making it are paid

14
00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:43.820
higher wages. Higher taxes can also cause inflation. When items are taxed, people who

15
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:50.940
produce goods don't want to see their profits go down. Instead, they raise their prices. This is

16
00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:58.060
called transferring the burden to the consumer. It means that producers make the same in profits,

17
00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:04.540
and the people buying the products are the ones who suffer. Inflation is complicated. Track the

18
00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:10.620
prices of some goods you are interested in and see if you can understand why they've changed over time.
